{"id":"mahabharata-3-025","work":"mahabharata","part":3,"partName":"आरण्यकपर्व","partNameEn":"Aranyaka Parva","unit":25,"title":"पञ्चविंशतितमोऽध्यायः","titleEn":"Adhyaya 25 · Life in the Dvaita forest","summary":{"en":"Yudhishthira asks Arjuna to choose a fit place to live for the twelve years, and they settle in the Dvaita forest by a lake. Brahmins, ascetics and Vedic reciters gather there around them.","kn":"ಹನ್ನೆರಡು ವರ್ಷ ವಾಸಕ್ಕೆ ತಕ್ಕ ಸ್ಥಳ ಆರಿಸೆಂದು ಯುಧಿಷ್ಠಿರನು ಅರ್ಜುನನಿಗೆ ಹೇಳುತ್ತಾನೆ; ಅವರು ದ್ವೈತವನದ ಸರೋವರದ ಬಳಿ ನೆಲೆಸುತ್ತಾರೆ. ಬ್ರಾಹ್ಮಣರು, ತಪಸ್ವಿಗಳು, ವೇದಪಾಠಕರು ಅವರ ಸುತ್ತ ಸೇರುತ್ತಾರೆ.","hi":"युधिष्ठिर अर्जुन से बारह वर्ष रहने के लिए उपयुक्त स्थान चुनने को कहते हैं, और वे द्वैतवन में एक सरोवर के पास बस जाते हैं। ब्राह्मण, तपस्वी और वेदपाठी वहाँ उनके चारों ओर एकत्र होते हैं।","te":"పన్నెండేళ్లు నివసించడానికి తగిన స్థలం ఎంచుకోమని యుధిష్ఠిరుడు అర్జునునికి చెబుతాడు; వారు ద్వైతవనంలో ఒక సరస్సు దగ్గర స్థిరపడతారు. బ్రాహ్మణులు, తాపసులు, వేదపాఠకులు వారి చుట్టూ చేరుతారు.","ta":"பன்னிரண்டு ஆண்டுகள் வாழத் தகுந்த இடத்தைத் தேர்ந்தெடுக்குமாறு யுதிஷ்டிரர் அர்ஜுனனிடம் சொல்ல, அவர்கள் த்வைத வனத்தில் ஒரு ஏரியருகே குடியேறுகிறார்கள். அந்தணர்களும் தவசிகளும் வேதம் ஓதுவோரும் அவர்களைச் சுற்றிக் கூடுகிறார்கள்.","ml":"പന്ത്രണ്ടു വർഷം താമസിക്കാൻ യോജിച്ച സ്ഥലം തിരഞ്ഞെടുക്കാൻ യുധിഷ്ഠിരൻ അർജുനനോട് ആവശ്യപ്പെടുന്നു; അവർ ഒരു തടാകത്തിനരികെ ദ്വൈതവനത്തിൽ താമസമുറപ്പിക്കുന്നു. ബ്രാഹ്മണരും തപസ്വികളും വേദപാരായണക്കാരും അവർക്ക് ചുറ്റും ഒത്തുകൂടുന്നു."},"source":"Mahabharata, Critical Edition (BORI, Pune) 3.25; e-text by M. Tokunaga and J. D. Smith, © BORI 1999, version of Mon Apr 11 2022","sections":[{"title":"कैरातपर्व","titleEn":"Kairata Parva (The mountain hunter)","verses":[{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":1,"text":"ततस्तेषु प्रयातेषु कौन्तेयः सत्यसंगरः ।\nअभ्यभाषत धर्मात्मा भ्रातॄन्सर्वान्युधिष्ठिरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"After they had gone, Yudhishthira, Kunti's son, true to his word and devout, spoke to all his brothers."}},{"n":2,"text":"द्वादशेमाः समास्माभिर्वस्तव्यं निर्जने वने ।\nसमीक्षध्वं महारण्ये देशं बहुमृगद्विजम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"We must live twelve years in a lonely forest. Look out in the great wilderness for a place with many animals and birds.\""}},{"n":3,"text":"बहुपुष्पफलं रम्यं शिवं पुण्यजनोचितम् ।\nयत्रेमाः शरदः सर्वाः सुखं प्रतिवसेमहि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Find a lovely, auspicious place rich in flowers and fruit, fit for holy people, where we can live happily through all these autumns.\""}},{"n":4,"text":"एवमुक्ते प्रत्युवाच धर्मराजं धनंजयः ।\nगुरुवन्मानवगुरुं मानयित्वा मनस्विनम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"When he had said this, Dhananjaya answered the king of dharma, honoring the wise lord of men as he would a teacher."}},{"text":"अर्जुन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Arjuna said:"}},{"n":5,"text":"भवानेव महर्षीणां वृद्धानां पर्युपासिता ।\nअज्ञातं मानुषे लोके भवतो नास्ति किंचन ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You yourself attend upon the elder great sages; nothing in the human world is unknown to you.\""}},{"n":6,"text":"त्वया ह्युपासिता नित्यं ब्राह्मणा भरतर्षभ ।\nद्वैपायनप्रभृतयो नारदश्च महातपाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"O best of the Bharatas, you have always served the brahmins, Dvaipayana and the rest, and the great ascetic Narada.\""}},{"n":7,"text":"यः सर्वलोकद्वाराणि नित्यं संचरते वशी ।\nदेवलोकाद्ब्रह्मलोकं गन्धर्वाप्सरसामपि ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Narada moves at will through all the doors of the worlds, from the world of the gods to the world of Brahma and to the Gandharvas and Apsarases.\""}},{"n":8,"text":"सर्वा गतीर्विजानासि ब्राह्मणानां न संशयः ।\nप्रभावांश्चैव वेत्थ त्वं सर्वेषामेव पार्थिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You know the paths of all the brahmins, without doubt, and you know, king, the powers of every one of them.\""}},{"n":9,"text":"त्वमेव राजञ्जानासि श्रेयःकारणमेव च ।\nयत्रेच्छसि महाराज निवासं तत्र कुर्महे ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"You alone, O king, know what is the cause of the highest good. So wherever you wish to live, there we will make our home.\""}},{"n":10,"text":"इदं द्वैतवनं नाम सरः पुण्यजनोचितम् ।\nबहुपुष्पफलं रम्यं नानाद्विजनिषेवितम् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Here is a holy lake called Dvaitavana, fit for holy people, lovely, rich in flowers and fruit, and frequented by many birds.\""}},{"n":11,"text":"अत्रेमा द्वादश समा विहरेमेति रोचये ।\nयदि तेऽनुमतं राजन्किं वान्यन्मन्यते भवान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"I would like us to spend these twelve years here. If you agree, O king, or if you think of something else, say so.\""}},{"text":"युधिष्ठिर उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Yudhishthira said:"}},{"n":12,"text":"ममाप्येतन्मतं पार्थ त्वया यत्समुदाहृतम् ।\nगच्छाम पुण्यं विख्यातं महद्द्वैतवनं सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"\"Partha, I too hold the view that you have put forward. Let us go to the great, renowned and holy lake of Dvaitavana.\""}},{"text":"वैशंपायन उवाच","meaning":{"en":"Vaishampayana said:"}},{"n":13,"text":"ततस्ते प्रययुः सर्वे पाण्डवा धर्मचारिणः ।\nब्राह्मणैर्बहुभिः सार्धं पुण्यं द्वैतवनं सरः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then all the Pandavas, devoted to dharma, set out for the holy Dvaitavana lake with many brahmins."}},{"n":14,"text":"ब्राह्मणाः साग्निहोत्राश्च तथैव च निरग्नयः ।\nस्वाध्यायिनो भिक्षवश्च सजपा वनवासिनः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There were brahmins who kept the sacred fires and those who did not, students of the Veda, mendicants, reciters of prayers, and forest dwellers."}},{"n":15,"text":"बहवो ब्राह्मणास्तत्र परिवव्रुर्युधिष्ठिरम् ।\nतपस्विनः सत्यशीलाः शतशः संशितव्रताः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Many brahmins gathered around Yudhishthira there, ascetics of true conduct, hundreds of them, firm in their vows."}},{"n":16,"text":"ते यात्वा पाण्डवास्तत्र बहुभिर्ब्राह्मणैः सह ।\nपुण्यं द्वैतवनं रम्यं विविशुर्भरतर्षभाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Together with these many brahmins, those Pandavas, best of the Bharatas, went and entered the holy and lovely Dvaitavana."}},{"n":17,"text":"तच्छालतालाम्रमधूकनीप\nकदम्बसर्जार्जुनकर्णिकारैः ।\nतपात्यये पुष्पधरैरुपेतं\nमहावनं राष्ट्रपतिर्ददर्श ॥","meaning":{"en":"The lord of the realm saw that great forest, full of sal, palmyra, mango, mahua, nipa, kadamba, sarja, arjuna and karnikara trees, bearing their flowers at the end of the hot season."}},{"n":18,"text":"महाद्रुमाणां शिखरेषु तस्थु-\nर्मनोरमां वाचमुदीरयन्तः ।\nमयूरदात्यूहचकोरसंघा-\nस्तस्मिन्वने काननकोकिलाश्च ॥","meaning":{"en":"On the tops of the great trees sat flocks of peacocks, datyuhas and chakoras, and forest cuckoos, uttering sweet cries in that forest."}},{"n":19,"text":"करेणुयूथैः सह यूथपानां\nमदोत्कटानामचलप्रभाणाम् ।\nमहान्ति यूथानि महाद्विपानां\nतस्मिन्वने राष्ट्रपतिर्ददर्श ॥","meaning":{"en":"In that forest the king saw great herds of mighty elephants, rutting and mountainlike, with their leaders and their cow-elephants."}},{"n":20,"text":"मनोरमां भोगवतीमुपेत्य\nधृतात्मनां चीरजटाधराणाम् ।\nतस्मिन्वने धर्मभृतां निवासे\nददर्श सिद्धर्षिगणाननेकान् ॥","meaning":{"en":"Coming to that lovely, pleasant place of self-controlled men wearing bark and matted locks, the abode of those who uphold dharma, he saw many hosts of siddhas and sages."}},{"n":21,"text":"ततः स यानादवरुह्य राजा\nसभ्रातृकः सजनः काननं तत् ।\nविवेश धर्मात्मवतां वरिष्ठ-\nस्त्रिविष्टपं शक्र इवामितौजाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Then the king, with his brothers and his people, got down from his vehicle and entered that forest, the best of the righteous, of boundless vigor, like Shakra entering heaven."}},{"n":22,"text":"तं सत्यसंधं सहिताभिपेतु-\nर्दिदृक्षवश्चारणसिद्धसंघाः ।\nवनौकसश्चापि नरेन्द्रसिंहं\nमनस्विनं संपरिवार्य तस्थुः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Gatherings of charanas and siddhas, eager to see that truthful man, came together, and the forest dwellers stood around that lion among kings, the wise lord."}},{"n":23,"text":"स तत्र सिद्धानभिवाद्य सर्वा-\nन्प्रत्यर्चितो राजवद्देववच्च ।\nविवेश सर्वैः सहितो द्विजाग्र्यैः\nकृताञ्जलिर्धर्मभृतां वरिष्ठः ॥","meaning":{"en":"There he greeted all the siddhas and was honored by them like a king and like a god; with folded hands, that best of dharma's upholders went in together with the foremost brahmins."}},{"n":24,"text":"स पुण्यशीलः पितृवन्महात्मा\nतपस्विभिर्धर्मपरैरुपेत्य ।\nप्रत्यर्चितः पुष्पधरस्य मूले\nमहाद्रुमस्योपविवेश राजा ॥","meaning":{"en":"That holy, great-souled king, like a father among the ascetics devoted to dharma, was honored by them and sat at the foot of a great flowering tree."}},{"n":25,"text":"भीमश्च कृष्णा च धनंजयश्च\nयमौ च ते चानुचरा नरेन्द्रम् ।\nविमुच्य वाहानवरुह्य सर्वे\nतत्रोपतस्थुर्भरतप्रबर्हाः ॥","meaning":{"en":"Bhima, Krishna, Dhananjaya, the twins and their attendants, setting aside the vehicles and dismounting, all stayed near the king, those best of the Bharatas."}},{"n":26,"text":"लतावतानावनतः स पाण्डवै-\nर्महाद्रुमः पञ्चभिरुग्रधन्विभिः ।\nबभौ निवासोपगतैर्महात्मभि-\nर्महागिरिर्वारणयूथपैरिव ॥","meaning":{"en":"That great tree, bent down with climbers and hanging creepers, shone with the five fierce archers, the Pandavas, who had come to live there, like a great mountain surrounded by a herd of elephants."}}]}]}